    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We have $(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) =$\n$1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ$\n$= (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = \\boxed{2}.$\nIn the third year of junior high school, students click on square tiles of each size on a computer screen, and the number of times a tile is clicked closely relates to the tile's side length. For example, if a tile's side length is $34^\\circ$, it is clicked 4 times; if a tile's side length is $58^\\circ$, it is clicked 2 times; if a tile's side length is $36^\\circ$, it is clicked 9 times. Therefore, a square tile with a side length of $x$ degrees is clicked $\\boxed{x^2}$ times.",
