      "text": "Given $P$ a point on the unit circle with an angle of 20 degrees, its projection on the axis - $P_1$ will be:\n\\[|O P'|= |O P|\\cos \\angle P O P_{1}|=\\frac{\\tan \\angle P O P_{1}}{\\sin \\angle P O P_{1}}=\\tan 20^\\circ.\\]\n\nGiven $Q$ a point on the unit circle with an angle of 25 degrees, its projection on the axis - $Q_1$ will be:\n\\[|O Q'|= |O Q|\\cos \\angle Q O Q_{1}|=\\frac{\\tan \\angle Q O Q_{1}}{\\sin \\angle Q O Q_{1}}=\\tan 25^\\circ.\\]\n\nThus,\n\\[..., P_1 = (P \\equiv 20^{\\circ}).\\]\nTaking the dot product of the vectors $O P'$ and $O Q'$, we get:\n\\[P_1 . Q_1 = |O P'|\\cdot |O Q'| \\cdot \\cos\\angle P O Q = \\tan 20^\\circ\\cdot\\tan 25^\\circ \\cdot \\cos 15^\\circ = \\sin 45^\\circ = \\boxed{1}.\\]\nNote by Ernest Koekemoer\nFebruary 8, 2020",
